<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>PrompTugal: the investment case</title>
<meta name="description" content="Why invest in PrompTugal: the next generation of news publishing, already running, from the Algarve. Investor deck 1, November 2026.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="deck.css"></head>
<body><main class="deck">

<!-- 1 · cover -->
<section class="slide pic">
  <img class="bg" src="img/hero-newsroom.jpg" alt="">
  <div class="veil"></div>
  <div class="head"><span><b>Investors</b> · deck 1</span><span>v1.1 · 7 November 2026</span></div>
  <div class="inner">
    <div class="kicker">An Algarvian startup · raising</div>
    <h1 style="font-size:104px">The next generation of news publishing is already running.</h1>
    <p class="lead">PrompTugal: a newsroom of people and AI agents that publishes accurate, sourced, signed news, sells time instead of attention, and tracks no one.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>The investment case · image: AI-made</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 2 · the problem -->
<section class="slide v ink">
  <div class="head"><span><b>The problem</b></span><span>02</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">The news industry is looking in the wrong direction</div>
  <h2>It sells the one thing whose price is going to zero: the article.</h2>
  <div class="cols c3" style="margin-top:70px">
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">01 · ADVERTISING</div><h3>The reader was the product</h3><p>Since the penny press of 1833. In 2005, 82% of American newspaper revenue was advertising. Then the web took the monopoly.</p></div>
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">02 · SUBSCRIPTIONS</div><h3>Then it went to rent</h3><p>"You pay 100% for the 10% you actually wanted." The industry's answer: more subscriptions, more personalisation behind the wall.</p></div>
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">03 · TRUST</div><h3>And readers walk away</h3><p>Trust in news at 37%; 42% avoid the news. American newsroom jobs fell 57% between 2008 and 2020.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="src" style="color:#9a978f;margin-top:40px">Figures as cited by Dinis Cruz in "The future of news is the story vault, not the paywall" (22 Sep 2026) and "The reader was always the product" (29 Sep 2026), newsroom.sgit.ai; trust and avoidance from the Reuters Institute, 2026.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>The investment case</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 3 · what readers want -->
<section class="slide v">
  <div class="head"><span><b>What people want</b></span><span>03</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">Accurate information, kept current, that saves time</div>
  <h2>The paper leads with it five times. Readers need it on fifty-seven days.</h2>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 1680 330" width="1680" height="330" style="margin-top:56px">
    <text x="0" y="28" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#595c64" letter-spacing="2">A LOCAL BRIDGE CLOSES · 57 DAYS UNTIL IT REOPENS · EACH SQUARE IS ONE DAY</text>
    <g transform="translate(0,56)">
      <!-- 57 days -->
      <g><rect x="0.0" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#c52830" opacity="1"/><rect x="57.6" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#c52830" opacity="1"/><rect x="115.2" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="172.8" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="230.4" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="288.0" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="345.6" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="403.2" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#c52830" opacity="1"/><rect x="460.8" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="518.4" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="576.0" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="633.6" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="691.2" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="748.8" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="806.4" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="864.0" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="921.6" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="979.2" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1036.8" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1094.4" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1152.0" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#c52830" opacity="1"/><rect x="1209.6" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1267.2" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1324.8" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1382.4" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1440.0" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1497.6" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1555.2" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1612.8" y="0" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="0.0" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="57.6" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="115.2" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="172.8" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="230.4" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="288.0" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="345.6" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="403.2" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="460.8" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="518.4" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="576.0" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="633.6" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="691.2" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="748.8" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="806.4" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="864.0" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="921.6" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#c52830" opacity="1"/><rect x="979.2" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1036.8" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1094.4" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1152.0" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1209.6" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1267.2" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1324.8" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1382.4" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1440.0" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1497.6" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/><rect x="1555.2" y="70" width="48" height="56" fill="#006600" opacity="0.85"/></g></g>
    <g transform="translate(0,230)" font-size="24">
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="28" height="28" fill="#c52830"/><text x="44" y="23" fill="#121317"><tspan font-weight="600">5 days</tspan> the paper leads with the story</text>
      <rect x="640" y="0" width="28" height="28" fill="#006600"/><text x="684" y="23" fill="#121317"><tspan font-weight="600">57 days</tspan> people need the current state: is it open, what detour, when</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-top:20px"><b>An article is written once. A maintained claim, kept current, is a service.</b> People will pay for accurate information that saves them time, not for a subscription to everything else.</p>
  <div class="src">From "The bridge, followed to the end" (Dinis Cruz, newsroom.sgit.ai, 7 Oct 2026): a worked simulation in a fictional town, quoted as written.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>The investment case</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 4 · our answer -->
<section class="slide v">
  <div class="head"><span><b>Our answer</b></span><span>04</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">PrompTugal</div>
  <h2>We sell time, the experience and trust. <span class="hl-red">Never the reader.</span></h2>
  <div class="cols c4" style="margin-top:70px">
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">TRUST</div><h3>Every fact sourced, every article signed</h3><p>Each fact carries its source and the date it was read; each article carries the cryptographic signature of whoever wrote it.</p></div>
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">TIME</div><h3>Value first, then pennies</h3><p>A starting credit, pence per page read. People pay because they already got something, not for a promise.</p></div>
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">PRIVACY</div><h3>No back end, no tracking</h3><p>Static and serverless. No IP, no cookie, no profile. Sign-in and personalisation run on the reader's side, in their own encrypted vault.</p></div>
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">SPEED</div><h3>People and agents, together</h3><p>A team of AI agents with names, keys, written limits and budgets, under a named human, released many times a day.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>The investment case</span></div>
</section>

