<!-- 7 · a week, because years -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>Velocity</b></span><span>07</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">Built in days, because of the years before it</div>
  <h2>Not a first attempt. The fifth newsroom, standing on all the others.</h2>
  <div class="tl" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(6,1fr)">
    <div class="ev"><div class="d">NOV 2024</div><h3>MyFeeds.ai</h3><p>Personalised briefings on semantic knowledge graphs, each item with its source.</p></div>
    <div class="ev"><div class="d">2025</div><h3>Trust and payment</h3><p>Ten long essays on provenance and paying for knowledge; micro and nano payments.</p></div>
    <div class="ev"><div class="d">TO MAR 2026</div><h3>sgit</h3><p>Encrypted vaults, keys and signatures: the layer every agent and reader uses.</p></div>
    <div class="ev"><div class="d">AUG 2026</div><h3>The Newsroom</h3><p>newsroom.sgit.ai: one editor and agents; pay per read live from 11 October.</p></div>
    <div class="ev"><div class="d">OCT 2026</div><h3>Events and a book</h3><p>Event and country newsrooms; a book written by nine agents and one editor.</p></div>
    <div class="ev now r"><div class="d">4 NOV 2026</div><h3>PrompTugal.news</h3><p>Everything above, reused, at the speed of an agentic team.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="vs" style="margin-top:70px;grid-template-columns:1fr 90px 1fr">
    <div class="side old"><h3>A competitor who forks our code</h3><p class="body">gets our position as of today.</p></div>
    <div class="mid">≠</div>
    <div class="side new"><h3>What they do not get</h3><p class="body">our velocity: the team, the method and the next hundred releases.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>The investment case · quote from open-source.sgit.ai</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 8 · what we sell -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>The business</b></span><span>08</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">Many revenue streams on one platform</div>
  <h2>We start with one: customisation at events. The rest follow.</h2>
  <div class="cols c4 tight" style="margin-top:40px;gap:24px">
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">01</div><h3>Pay per use</h3><p>Micropayments after the value: pence per page from a starting credit.</p></div>
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">02</div><h3>Customisation</h3><p>A person's or a team's own version: their day, briefings before and after each talk.</p></div>
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">03</div><h3>Other events</h3><p>The same platform for any event: data before, during and after.</p></div>
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">04</div><h3>The team, deployed</h3><p>The agentic team for a project, an event or a body of content.</p></div>
    <div class="card r"><div class="n">05</div><h3>Agentic workflows</h3><p>Taught and installed for companies that want to run their own, safely.</p></div>
    <div class="card r"><div class="n">06</div><h3>Data for agents</h3><p>Feeds, triplets, JSON and graph objects that make agents faster and cheaper.</p></div>
    <div class="card r"><div class="n">07</div><h3>Intelligence packs</h3><p>Who is who in AI in Portugal, mapped and kept current.</p></div>
    <div class="card r"><div class="n">08</div><h3>Licensing</h3><p>Dual licensing: our open-source technology under a company's own terms, maintained by us.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="src" style="margin-top:22px">Where we start: 01 and 02 at Web Summit (readers paying after the value; teams and delegations wanting their own version). 03 and 04 follow at the next events; 05 to 08 once those sell. On sale today: the reading top-up.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>The investment case</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 9 · value before payment -->
<section class="slide pic lightpic">
  <img class="bg" src="img/hero-time.jpg" alt="" style="object-position:right center">
  <div class="veil light"></div>
  <div class="head"><span><b>Pay after the value</b></span><span>09</span></div>
  <div class="inner" style="max-width:1000px">
    <div class="kicker">The model, in one line</div>
    <h2 style="font-size:72px">Others ask people to pay for future value. We let them have the value first.</h2>
    <ul class="ticks" style="margin-top:44px">
      <li><b>Come for the summit:</b> find the talks you would have missed, where to go, who is there.</li>
      <li><b>Spend time, learn something,</b> come back tomorrow.</li>
      <li><b>By the time you pay,</b> a few pence a page, you are already glad you did, and you top up.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>The investment case · image: AI-made</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 10 · profitable -->
<section class="slide v">
  <div class="head"><span><b>Why it can be profitable</b></span><span>10</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">Provide services and be profitable</div>
  <h2>A platform that costs very little to run, and a team that does the repeatable work.</h2>
  <div class="cols c3" style="margin-top:64px">
    <div class="stat"><div class="v" style="font-size:72px">No servers</div><div class="l">for readers: pages built from data, served statically and serverless. The stack costs very little.</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="v" style="font-size:72px">A new edition</div><div class="l">is a configuration and a team, not a newsroom of hires: an event, a sector, a country, a language.</div></div>
    <div class="stat r"><div class="v" style="font-size:72px">Never</div><div class="l">advertising, tracking or paying for coverage. Trust is the asset; we do not spend it.</div></div>
  </div>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-top:70px">Open source by strategy, not charity: code Apache-2.0, text CC BY 4.0. What we sell is <b>the running, maintained, certified service</b>, and a licence on a company's own terms when it wants one.</p>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>The investment case</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 11 · founder strategy -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>The founder's strategy</b></span><span>11</span></div>
  <div class="cols w40 center" style="height:100%;margin-top:0">
    <div>
      <div class="kicker">Many startups, one strategy</div>
      <h2 style="font-size:66px">Having many startups is the point: each is built on the others.</h2>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size:30px">Dinis Cruz runs several open-source startups under one written strategy. PrompTugal is the newest, and the first built from all of them at once.</p>
      <div class="src">open-source.sgit.ai · "open source is a strategy, not a charity"</div>
